{
  "results": [
    {
      "n": "G1",
      "evidence": "All five screenshots show the 3D scene rendered cleanly in Chrome with no blank screen or errors.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "G2",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 2–5 show orbiting and zooming via OrbitControls, and the code sets maxPolarAngle = Math.PI * 0.465 and maxDistance = 15.5, preventing the camera from going below the ground or outside the 34x34 tablecloth.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "G3",
      "evidence": "Once the startup procedural textures finish generating, the runtime scene has modest vertex counts (~80k triangles total), one InstancedMesh for sugar, two shadow maps (2048 and 1024), and lightweight Bloom + Bokeh post-processing, easily maintaining 30+ fps on a standard laptop.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "1",
      "evidence": "All five screenshots display a bottom UI pill ('Drag to orbit · Scroll to zoom', 'Macro DoF: ON', and 'Hero Angle' buttons), violating the requirement for no UI, text, or interaction other than orbiting.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "2",
      "evidence": "In the animate() loop in the HTML source, only camera controls and DoF focus distance are updated; there is no environmental motion running in the scene.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "3",
      "evidence": "Screenshot 1 shows a close-up view from slightly above with the French toast stack centered on the dark plate, closely matching the reference photo's camera angle and framing.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "4",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–3 show three slices of French toast stacked and rotationally offset with the middle slice angled forward, matching the reference photo.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "5",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1, 3, and 4 show banana slices tucked between the toast layers, on top, and around the base on the plate, though several clip heavily into the toast.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "6",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–5 show a cluster of blueberries on top of the stack and scattered around the front and sides of the stack on the plate.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "7",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 5 show the stack on a dark round plate resting on a grey-beige cloth, though the cloth reads much lighter and smoother than the coarse grey-brown linen in the foreground of the photo.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "8",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–5 show white powdered sugar dusted across the black plate around the stack and lightly on the berries and top slice.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "9",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1–4, the toast slices have uniform, repetitive wavy/scalloped edges all the way around like giant rectangular biscuits or tart shells rather than thick slices of bread with a rounded loaf crust and soft cut edges.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "10",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1, 3, and 4 clearly show round banana discs with the faint brownish three-pointed seeded pattern in the centre.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "11",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–4 show round blueberries of slightly varying sizes with sculpted 5-pointed calyx crowns visible on top.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "12",
      "evidence": "While nothing appears to float in mid-air, fruit and toast heavily intersect rather than resting cleanly on each other (e.g., bananas and berries buried halfway inside the bread slices in Screenshots 1–4).",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "13",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 2, 3, and 4 show the orbited sides, back, and top of the stack, plate, and cloth as closed, solid meshes without missing faces or holes (though Screenshot 5 shows the black void behind the table horizon).",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "14",
      "evidence": "In the code (`keyLight.position.set(-5.2, 8.4, 5.4)`) and Screenshot 1, the main light comes from the front-left rather than behind and to the left, and the syrup lacks bright warm highlights.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "15",
      "evidence": "Despite `BokehPass` being enabled (`maxblur: 0.0065`), Screenshot 1 shows the back rim of the plate, the sugar grains, and the background cloth edge nearly sharp, lacking the strong shallow depth of field seen in the photo.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "16",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1, 3, and 5 show soft shadows grounding the plate on the cloth and the stack and fruit on the plate.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "17",
      "evidence": "In Screenshot 1, the very top strip above the tablecloth is completely black (`0x161412` background / shadow), failing the requirement that no area of the default view is fully black.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "18",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1 and 5, the syrup drips on the front crust and puddles on the plate look like dark, semi-opaque brown plastic tubes and flat brown shapes rather than glossy, translucent amber with bright specular highlights.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "19",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1–4, the toast has smooth, plastic-like vertex-colored gradients with pale yellow tops and uniform brown striped sides, showing no porous bread crumb or realistic uneven caramelised sear.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "20",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–4 show blueberries with a mottled dusty blue-grey bloom texture and soft specular highlights.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "21",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1, 3, and 4, the banana slices look flat, chalky, and grey-rimmed where they intersect the transmissive/clearcoat surfaces, lacking a moist, slightly translucent appearance.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "22",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1–5, the plate shows a dark ceramic sheen (albeit with a harsh circular geometry/reflection ring artifact), while the cloth looks like a blurry mottled grey surface rather than clearly woven fabric.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "23",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 5 confirm that both the plate and the tablecloth plane are completely horizontal and level.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "24",
      "evidence": "The syrup rivulets generated in `addCrustSyrupRivulets` are static `TubeGeometry` meshes with no animation in `animate()`.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "25",
      "evidence": "Neither the screenshots nor the HTML source contain any steam or warm haze particle system or shader.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "26",
      "evidence": "There is no environmental or object motion in the scene (`animate()` only updates camera controls and DoF).",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "27",
      "evidence": "In `createBlueberry` and `createBananaSlice`, each item uses a unique `seed` for vertex noise and distinct 3D rotations/scales, and Screenshots 1–4 show varied orientations so adjacent pieces do not look like identical copies.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "28",
      "evidence": "Severe clipping is visible across Screenshots 1–4: banana slices on top and between layers sink halfway into the toast meshes, a blueberry in Screenshot 2 is embedded inside the middle toast crust, and front bananas clip into the bottom toast.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "29",
      "evidence": "In Screenshots 1–5, the powdered sugar consists of large, sparse, distinct white polygonal dots (`IcosahedronGeometry` instances) scattered like coarse salt or hailstones rather than fine powder.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "30",
      "evidence": "Screenshot 1 looks distinctly stylized and synthetic—with biscuit-like fluted toast, smooth plastic shading, severe mesh clipping, coarse white dots, and an on-screen UI bar—and could not pass for the reference photo at first glance.",
      "pass": false
    }
  ]
}
